{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And all humankind.</b> The indefinite word אדם throughout all of Scripture includes men, women, and children. And if you ask: how was the generation of the flood punished, since they were not commanded concerning the commandments? One may answer: there are several commandments that people are obligated to observe by force of reason, even though they were not commanded, and therefore they were punished — like Cain, who was punished for bloodshed even though he was not commanded concerning this. Or perhaps they were commanded about robbery itself."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:22.441950753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}